<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,One of the production assistants remarked that she expected more money to be allocated to set design for dramas.,1,drama,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize set design in the budget allocation for drama films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,You overheard a crew member question why the studio isn't pouring their resources into set design for a project like this.,1,drama,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize set design in the budget allocation for drama films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,A member of the effects team remarked that <pick:the special effects budget seemed surprisingly modest for an action blockbuster|he expected far more resources for special effects than there actually were|the production's ambitions exceeded what the special effects budget could realistically support>.,3,action,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize special effects in the budget allocation for action films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,One of the assistant directors commented that <pick:audiences expect cutting-edge special effects from action films these days|modern action movies live or die by the quality of their effects|viewers would notice immediately if the special effects looked cheap>.,3,action,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize special effects in the budget allocation for action films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"You overheard a social media manager wonder <pick:how you're planning to get people talking about the comedy without a bigger marketing campaign|why you aren't leaning harder into promoting the film's humor|whether the comedy would reach audiences with so little advertising|why there wasn't enough money allocated for trailers, clips, and promotional events needed for a comedy release>.",3,comedy,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize marketing in the budget allocation for comedy films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,You overheard a crew member question <pick:why trailers that actually sell the laughs aren't being prioritized|why marketing doesn't have the resources to convince audiences that this comedy stands out|why so little funding was being devoted to advertising the film's funniest moments>.,3,comedy,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize marketing in the budget allocation for comedy films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,An effects artist commented that <pick:studios generally dedicate much larger effects budgets to fantasy films because audiences expect convincing magic|the dragons and magical creatures deserved a much larger effects budget|a fantasy epic should be spending much more on special effects than on anything else>.,3,fantasy,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize special effects in the budget allocation for fantasy films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,You overheard a camera operator wonder <pick:how you're planning to stage magical battles without investing more in special effects|whether the spellcasting would feel convincing with such a poor budget|how the film expects audiences to believe its magical world without investing more in special effects>.,3,fantasy,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize special effects in the budget allocation for fantasy films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"An art department assistant commented that <pick:a horror movie like this should have invested far more in creating unsettling environments|the sets didn't seem to receive enough funding to create a truly frightening haunted house|more funding should have been allocated to creating detailed monster costumes and unsettling character designs|she expected more resources for the sets, props, costumes, and creature details>.",4,horror,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for horror films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"You overheard a set decorator wonder <pick:how he's supposed to make the locations feel haunted without more money for set dressing and design|why you're opposed to creating detailed, disturbing environments, considering the funds she's been given|whether audiences will feel immersed when the sets and backgrounds are so limited>.",3,horror,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for horror films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"A production designer commented that <pick:musicals rely on imaginative sets, detailed costumes, and striking environments to create memorable moments|the film's performance spaces needed far more investment to feel spectacular|the musical's visual world needed a much larger budget to match the scale of the songs and choreography>.",3,musical,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for musical films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,One of the assistant directors wondered <pick:why you're not spending more on making ordinary locations into impressive musical settings|whether the limited design budget would limit the scale of the dance sequences|if the production should have prioritized using its funds to help create elaborate set pieces for each major song|if the songs would have a stronger impact with more ambitious production design funding to support them>.,3,musical,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for musical films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"You overheard an art department assistant say <pick:the sets wouldn't have the funding needed to create the right mood of danger and uncertainty|he expected more resources to build the film’s tense, mysterious world|that if production design had more funding, things like fog machines could be added to the set>.",3,thriller,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for thriller films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,A production designer was embarrassed <pick:to have to use cheaper props and recycled set pieces because of the production budget|that his crew would have to borrow and repurpose items rather than create a unique look for the thriller|he'd have to leave out many background details that would have made the locations feel more unsettling|that the crew would have to spend more time hiding budget limitations than designing sets properly>.,3,thriller,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for thriller films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"One of the production assistants scoffed, saying <pick:he expected more funding would go toward building detailed saloons, dusty streets, and frontier settlements|the film needed more resources to recreate the Old West vibe|the studio should've invested more into building a believable frontier world|the Western wouldn't feel authentic with such limited production design resources>.",3,western,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for western films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"One of the costume assistants remarked that <pick:he expected more money to be spent on creating distinct Western wardrobes for each character|the clothing budget seemed too limited for a film that relies on its period look|the studio should have invested more in authentic boots, hats, coats, and frontier clothing|the production design was missing opportunities to make the characters feel rooted in the era>.",3,western,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for western films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,One of the set designers expressed that <pick:money should've been given to production design so they could remake historical landmarks featured throughout the film|the production design budget seemed too limited to recreate the scale of the historical setting|several set builds would have to be dropped because the production design budget was too low|liberties would have to be taken with historical accuracy due to the production design budget>.,3,historical,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for historical films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,"You overheard a crew member say that <pick:it didn't make sense for a historical film to cut corners on production design|this kind of film depended on believable period environments, not marketing or special effects|the production design budget had clearly been squeezed|the film was asking production design to do far too much with far too little>.",3,historical,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize production design in the budget allocation for historical films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,You overheard someone from the distribution team say <pick:the studio was leaving too much potential on the table by limiting promotion|marketing was being treated as an afterthought despite the film's genre|the studio should do more to highlight the film's emotional core in its marketing>.,3,romance,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize marketing in the budget allocation for romance films.,,,,,,,
<reference:movie_director_budget_feedback>,You overheard a crew member say that <pick:the studio was spending too little on making audiences aware of the film|a romance movie like this can't succeed without a stronger marketing effort|it's surprising marketing wasn't getting more support to reach viewers who would connect with the story>.,2,romance,,,I began wondering whether I should prioritize marketing in the budget allocation for romance films.,,,,,,,
